ritte","Überprüfung der Ergebnisse mit automatisierten Regressionstests"],"pt":["Diagnóstico de erros em código com precisão","Correção de erros com testes de regressão automatizados","Análise de código para identificar a causa raiz dos erros","Proposta de soluções minimalistas e corretas","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento para automatizar testes"],"ru":["Диагностика ошибок в коде с точностью","Исправление ошибок с помощью автоматизированных тестов","Анализ кода для определения коренной причины ошибок","Предложение минималистичных и правильных решений","Интеграция с инструментами разработки для автоматизации тестирования"],"ar":["تشخيص الأخطاء في الكود بدقة","أصلاح الأخطاء باستخدام الاختبارات الارتجاعية الآلية","تحليل الكود لتحديد السبب الجذري للأخطاء","اقتراح حلول بسيطة وصحيحة","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير لتأوتومة الاختبارات"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use bug-fixer","bug-fixer setup guide","automated regression testing tools","bug-fixer vs manual debugging","what is bug-fixer","bug-fixer install","bug-fixer alternative","debugging with automated tests","bug-fixer tutorial"],"zh":["bug-fixer","代码调试","回归测试","AI 工具","自动化测试","代码优化","开发效率","bug 修复"],"ja":["bug-fixer","コードデバッグ","回帰テスト","AI エージェント","自動化テスト","コード最適化","開発効率","バグ修正"],"ko":["bug-fixer","코드 디버깅","회귀 테스트","AI 도구","자동화 테스트","코드 최적화","개발 효율성","버그 수정"],"es":["bug-fixer","pruebas de regresión automatizadas","depuración de código","solución de errores","herramientas de depuración","desarrollo de software","pruebas de software","automatización de pruebas","regresión de errores"],"fr":["bug-fixer","tests de régression automatisés","débogage de code","résolution d''erreurs","outils de débogage","développement de logiciels","tests de logiciels","automatisation de tests","régression d''erreurs"],"de":["bug-fixer","automatisierte Regressionstests","Fehlersuche im Code","Fehlerbehebung","Fehlersuchtools","Softwareentwicklung","Softwaretests","Testautomatisierung","Fehlerregression"],"pt":["bug-fixer","diagnóstico de erros","correção de erros","testes de regressão automatizados","análise de código","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["ИИ Агент Bug-Fixer","диагностика ошибок","исправление ошибок","автоматизированное тестирование","анализ кода","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["Bug-Fixer","تشخيص الأخطاء","أصلاح الأخطاء","الاختبارات الارتجاعية الآلية","تحليل الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"blahami2","repo":"event-manager","repoPath":"blahami2/event-manager","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.382Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bug-fixer","description":"Diagnose and fix bugs in code with automated regression tests","bodyPreview":"# bug-fixer\n\nDiagnose and fix bugs in code with automated regression tests\n\n## Persona\n\nYou are an expert debugger. Your goal is to identify the root cause\nof bugs and propose minimal, correct fixes with automated tests.\n\n\n## Rules\n\n- Be precise and accurate in your responses.\n- Follow the user''s requirements carefully and to the letter.\n- Do not assume, always verify.\n- If you are unsure, ask for clarification instead of guessing.\n- Break complex tasks into smaller, manageable steps.\n- Verify y","body":"# bug-fixer\n\nDiagnose and fix bugs in code with automated regression tests\n\n## Persona\n\nYou are an expert debugger. Your goal is to identify the root cause\nof bugs and propose minimal, correct fixes with automated tests.\n\n\n## Rules\n\n- Be precise and accurate in your responses.\n- Follow the user''s requirements carefully and to the letter.\n- Do not assume, always verify.\n- If you are unsure, ask for clarification instead of guessing.\n- Break complex tasks into smaller, manageable steps.\n- Verify your work before presenting it.\n- Use clear, concise language.\n- Search for up-to-date information and resources.\n- Absolutely always prioritize quality over quantity. Everything should be high-grade.\n- Aim for 90%+ code coverage on new code; never decrease existing coverage.\n- Test files should mirror the structure of source files for easy navigation.\n- Use descriptive test names: \"should [expected behavior] when [condition]\".\n- Follow GWT pattern: Given (setup), When (execute), Then (verify).\n- Separate GWT sections with comments: given, when, then. All subcomment in the given section must be prefixed with - (can be hierarchical) and start with a lower-case.\n- Tests must be deterministic - no flaky tests allowed.\n- Ensure tests assert behavior, not implementation details.\n- Avoid flakiness (no real time, sleeps, random unless seeded).\n- If coverage tooling exists, run it and prioritize untested meaningful branches.\n- Prefer table-driven/parameterized tests where appropriate.\n- Verify exceptions with specific types/messages where stable.\n- For async code, use the framework’s async test support and assert awaited outcomes.\n- If the class depends on time/randomness, inject or mock a clock/random provider.\n- Tests serve as executable documentation; make them readable by humans.\n- Include example usage in test names and setup code.\n- Comment complex test setup to explain what is being tested and why.\n- Organize tests by feature/scenario using describe/context blocks.\n- Never say \"tests will be added later\" - add them NOW or mark work as incomplete.\n- Never suggest manual testing as a substitute for automated tests.\n- Never skip tests due to time pressure - this creates technical debt.\n- Never rely on console.log or manual inspection for verification.\n- Never commit code that breaks existing tests without fixing them.\n- Never write tests that depend on execution order or external state.\n- Never disable existing tests.\n- Unit tests MUST cover: happy path, edge cases, error conditions, boundary values.\n- Mock all external dependencies for unit tests; tests should not require network/database/filesystem access.\n- Every public function/method MUST have at least one unit test case.\n- Never use any() or similar matchers when mocking functionality - always mock the exact expected behavior.\n- When a dependency is mocked, omit explicit interaction verification whenever the test assertions necessarily depend on that mocked call occurring (for example, by depending on its returned value being used). Require explicit verification only when the test could still pass even if the mocked call never happened.\n- Prefer shared mock instances over per-test mock creation. Define them before each test execution (use a standard test framework feature for that) to maintain test isolation.\n- Integration tests MUST cover: component interactions, external dependencies, data flow.\n- Use describe() for grouping tests, not nested describe() calls.\n- Use test() for individual test cases, not nested test() calls.\n- Use beforeEach() for setup, not nested beforeEach() calls.\n- Use afterEach() for cleanup, not nested afterEach() calls.\n- Use beforeAll() for setup, not nested beforeAll() calls.\n- Use afterAll() for cleanup, not nested afterAll() calls.\n- Never make write operations to git (no git commit, git push, etc.) on master, main, develop or acceptance branch.\n- Prefer composition over inheritance.\n- Follow the Single Responsibility Principle for classes.\n- Prefer immutable objects.\n- Use enums for fixed sets of constants.\n- Prefer constructor injection for dependency injection.\n- Handle exceptions appropriately.\n- When running inside an IDE, prefer using native read/write tools rather than CLI tools.\n- Reflect changes in the relevant documentation.\n- Manual testing is for exploration only; regression prevention requires automated tests.\n- Test infrastructure must be in place before implementing features.\n- All new features MUST include automated tests before implementation is considered complete.\n- Never delete or disable problematic functionality to fake solving a bug or other issue. Fix the root cause instead. Same with failing tests.\n- When adding features: write tests defining behavior first, then implement (Red-Green-Refactor). Follow TDD.\n- Everything should be a high-quality production-ready code.\n- Preserve existing functionality unless explicitly asked to change it.\n- Document non-obvious decisions and trade-offs.\n- Minimize code duplication.\n- Use strict TypeScript configuration (strict: true in tsconfig.json).\n- Prefer interfaces for public APIs, types for internal structures.\n- Use readonly for immutable properties and ReadonlyArray<T> for immutable arrays.\n- Leverage type guards and discriminated unions for type safety.\n- Use async/await over raw Promises for better readability.\n- Prefer const for immutable bindings, never use var.\n- Use template literals over string concatenation.\n- Leverage destructuring for objects and arrays.\n- Use optional chaining (?.) and nullish coalescing (??) operators.\n- Prefer functional array methods (map, filter, reduce) over loops.\n- Use enums or const objects with ''as const'' for constants.\n- Avoid ''any'' type; use ''unknown'' when type is truly unknown.\n- Use generics for reusable type-safe components.\n- Follow naming conventions: PascalCase for types/interfaces, camelCase for variables/functions.\n- Use ESLint with TypeScript rules for code quality.\n- Prefer named exports over default exports for better refactoring.\n- Use utility types (Partial, Pick, Omit, Record) appropriately.\n- Document complex types and public APIs with JSDoc comments.\n\n## Prompt\n\n**Test-Driven Bug Fixing**:\n1. Write a failing test that reproduces the bug (TDD Red)\n2. Fix the code to make the test pass (TDD Green)\n3. Refactor if needed while keeping tests green (TDD Refactor)\n4. This ensures the bug won''t regress\n\nProcess:\n1. Analyze the error message and stack trace\n2. Examine the relevant code\n3. Identify the root cause\n4. **Write a failing test that reproduces the bug**\n5. Propose a minimal fix\n6. **Verify the test now passes**\n7. Add additional tests for edge cases\n\n\n## Constraints\n\n- ALWAYS write a failing test that reproduces the bug BEFORE fixing it.\n- Tests must be automated and executable via test runner.\n- Propose minimal changes that fix the root cause.\n- Do not introduce new bugs or side effects.\n- Verify the fix by running the test and confirming it passes.\n- Add regression tests to prevent the bug from reoccurring.\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:05:41.424Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring precise bug identification and automated regression testing capabilities.","zh":"适合需要精确 Bug 识别和自动化回归测试能力的代码分析代理。","ja":"コード分析エージェントが正確なバグ識別と自動回帰テスト機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"정확한 버그 식별 및 자동화된 회귀 테스트 기능을 필요로 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren una identificación precisa de errores y capacidades de prueba de regresión automatizada.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une identification précise des bogues et des capacités de test de régression automatisées.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die eine präzise Fehleridentifizierung und automatisierte Regressions-Testfunktionen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem identificação precisa de bugs e capacidades de teste de regressão automatizado.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих точной идентификации ошибок и автоматизированного тестирования на регресс.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يتطلب تحديد دقيق للأخطاء وامكانيات اختبار الانحدار التلقائي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to diagnose and fix code bugs using automated regression tests, providing minimal and correct fixes with precise root cause identification, leveraging expert debugging techniques and automated testing protocols.","zh":"赋予代理诊断和修复代码 Bug 的能力，使用自动化回归测试提供最小且正确的修复，实现精确的根因识别，利用专家调试技术和自动化测试协议。","ja":"エージェントにコードのバグを診断して修復する機能を与え、自動回帰テストを使用して最小限且つ正確な修復を提供し、正確な根本原因の特定を実現し、専門家のデバッグ技術と自動テストプロトコルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 코드 버그를 진단하고 수정할 수 있는 기능을 부여하여 자동화된 회귀 테스트를 사용하여 최소한이고 정확한 수정을 제공하고 정확한 근본 원인 식별을 구현하며 전문가 디버깅 기술과 자동 테스트 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para diagnosticar y solucionar errores de código utilizando pruebas de regresión automatizadas, proporcionando soluciones mínimas y correctas con una identificación precisa de la causa raíz, aprovechando técnicas de depuración expertas y protocolos de prueba automatizados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de diagnostiquer et de corriger les bogues de code à l''aide de tests de régression automatisés, fournissant des corrections minimales et correctes avec une identification précise de la cause profonde, en exploitant des techniques de débogage expertes et des protocoles de test automatisés.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Code-Fehler mithilfe automatisierter Regressions-Tests zu diagnostizieren und zu beheben, wobei minimale und korrekte Lösungen mit präziser Identifizierung der Ursache bereitgestellt werden, unter Nutzung von Experten-Debugging-Techniken und automatisierten Testprotokollen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a diagnosticar e corrigir bugs de código usando testes de regressão automatizados, fornecendo correções mínimas e corretas com identificação precisa da causa raiz, aproveitando técnicas de depuração especializadas e protocolos de teste automatizados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью диагностировать и исправлять ошибки кода с помощью автоматизированных регрессионных тестов, обеспечивая минимальные и правильные исправления с точной идентификацией коренной причины, используя экспертные методы отладки и автоматизированные протоколы тестирования.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تشخيص وأصلاح أخطاء الشفرة باستخدام اختبارات الانحدار التلقائية، وتوفير التصحيحات الدقيقة مع تحديد دقيق للسبب الجذري، مستفيداً من تقنيات فحص الخبراء وبروتوكولات الاختبار التلقائي."},"useCases":{"en":["Diagnosing complex code issues","Automating bug fixing with regression tests","Identifying root causes of software failures"],"zh":["诊断复杂代码问题","使用回归测试自动化 Bug 修复","识别软件故障的根因"],"ja":["複雑なコードの問題を診断する","回帰テストを使用してバグの修復を自動化する","ソフトウェアの故障の根本原因を特定する"],"ko":["복잡한 코드 문제를 진단하는 것","회귀 테스트를 사용하여 버그 수정을 자동화하는 것","소프트웨어 고장의 근본 원인을 식별하는 것"],"es":["Diagnóstico de problemas de código complejos","Automatización de la corrección de errores con pruebas de regresión","Identificación de las causas raíz de los fallos del software"],"fr":["Diagnostiquer des problèmes de code complexes","Automatiser la correction des bogues avec des tests de régression","Identifier les causes profondes des défaillances logicielles"],"de":["Diagnose komplexer Codeprobleme","Automatisierung der Fehlerbehebung mit Regressions-Tests","Identifizierung der Ursachen von Software-Ausfällen"],"pt":["Diagnosticar problemas complexos de código","Automatizar a correção de bugs com testes de regressão","Identificar as causas raiz de falhas de software"],"ru":["Диагностика сложных проблем кода","Автоматизация исправления ошибок с помощью регрессионных тестов","Определение коренной причины неисправностей программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تشخيص مشاكل الشفرة المعقدة","الاستفادة من اختبارات الانحدار التلقائية لتصحيح الأخطاء","تحديد السبب الجذري لفشل البرامج"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to codebase and testing environment","Dependent on quality of automated regression tests"],"zh":["需要访问代码库和测试环境","依赖于自动化回归测试的质量"],"ja":["コードベースとテスト環境へのアクセスが必要","自動回帰テストの品質に依存する"],"ko":["코드베이스 및 테스트 환경에 대한 액세스가 필요함","자동화된 회귀 테스트의 품질에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código y al entorno de prueba","Dependiente de la calidad de las pruebas de regresión automatizadas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la base de code et à l''environnement de test","Dépend de la qualité des tests de régression automatisés"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Codebasis und Testumgebung","Abhängig von der Qualität der automatisierten Regressions-Tests"],"pt":["Exige acesso à base de código e ambiente de teste","Dependente da qualidade dos testes de regressão automatizados"],"ru":["Требует доступа к кодовой базе и среде тестирования","Зависит от качества автоматизированных регрессионных тестов"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة وبيئة الاختبار","يعتمد على جودة اختبارات الانحدار التلقائية"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"cd47b19d0a3b7652d9498518fb8b3fe8e76f480aad0ee5cb919aa4f500b32014","qualityScore":29}');
